WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.791
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online TOEFL preparation.

2
00:00:06.091 --> 00:00:09.455
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.755 --> 00:00:19.338
Unit one: TOEFL iBT Overview and Scores. Today you will understand the new TOEFL iBT sections, timing and the 1-6 score scale.

4
00:00:19.638 --> 00:00:22.151
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:26.043
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:26.883 --> 00:00:27.722
Section.

7
00:00:28.717 --> 00:00:31.273
Section means one main part of the test.

8
00:00:31.883 --> 00:00:33.593
Reading is the first section.

9
00:00:34.183 --> 00:00:36.638
Your turn. Say: Section.

10
00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:40.559
Section.

11
00:00:41.317 --> 00:00:42.434
Adaptive.

12
00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:45.902
Adaptive means changing to match your level.

13
00:00:46.517 --> 00:00:48.505
The Reading section is adaptive.

14
00:00:49.117 --> 00:00:52.164
Your turn. Say: Adaptive.

15
00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:55.908
Adaptive.

16
00:00:56.650 --> 00:00:57.454
Band.

17
00:00:58.450 --> 00:01:00.763
Band means a level on a score scale.

18
00:01:01.350 --> 00:01:03.524
I need a band of 5.0.

19
00:01:04.117 --> 00:01:06.537
Your turn. Say: Band.

20
00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:10.320
Band.

21
00:01:11.083 --> 00:01:11.899
Scale.

22
00:01:12.883 --> 00:01:15.359
Scale means a range of numbers used to measure.

23
00:01:15.950 --> 00:01:17.915
The scale goes from 1 to 6.

24
00:01:18.517 --> 00:01:20.751
Your turn. Say: Scale.

25
00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:24.671
Scale.

26
00:01:25.417 --> 00:01:26.220
Task.

27
00:01:27.217 --> 00:01:30.261
Task means a single question type or activity.

28
00:01:30.850 --> 00:01:32.850
Each task has its own format.

29
00:01:33.450 --> 00:01:35.998
Your turn. Say: Task.

30
00:01:38.833 --> 00:01:39.695
Task.

31
00:01:40.450 --> 00:01:41.381
Average.

32
00:01:42.383 --> 00:01:44.975
Average means the result of adding and dividing.

33
00:01:45.583 --> 00:01:47.676
The overall score is the average.

34
00:01:48.283 --> 00:01:50.727
Your turn. Say: Average.

35
00:01:53.567 --> 00:01:54.405
Average.

36
00:01:55.150 --> 00:01:56.023
CEFR.

37
00:01:57.017 --> 00:02:00.154
CEFR means the European levels from A1 to C2.

38
00:02:00.750 --> 00:02:02.459
The scale links to CEFR.

39
00:02:03.050 --> 00:02:05.621
Your turn. Say: CEFR.

40
00:02:08.467 --> 00:02:09.595
CEFR.

41
00:02:10.350 --> 00:02:11.502
Requirement.

42
00:02:12.517 --> 00:02:15.480
Requirement means something a university asks for.

43
00:02:16.083 --> 00:02:18.025
Check the university requirement.

44
00:02:18.617 --> 00:02:20.944
Your turn. Say: Requirement.

45
00:02:23.800 --> 00:02:24.906
Requirement.

46
00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:29.351
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:30.217 --> 00:02:33.308
Visal, what is new about TOEFL iBT now?

48
00:02:34.417 --> 00:02:44.244
The test is about ninety minutes, much shorter than before. Reading and Listening are adaptive, so the questions change to match your performance.

49
00:02:45.350 --> 00:02:46.874
How long is each section?

50
00:02:47.983 --> 00:03:00.365
Reading is about thirty minutes, Listening twenty-nine, Writing twenty-three and Speaking eight. Each section has different task types, so you must learn them one by one.

51
00:03:01.450 --> 00:03:03.055
How is the score reported?

52
00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:17.704
Each section gets a band from 1 to 6 in half-point steps, and the overall score is the average. The bands connect to the CEFR levels, and score reports may also show the older scale for a time.

53
00:03:18.867 --> 00:03:20.576
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:21.417 --> 00:03:25.750
Grammar focus: Strategy: know the format before you practise.

55
00:03:26.050 --> 00:03:27.271
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:27.983 --> 00:03:31.724
Reading and Listening are adaptive, so the difficulty changes.

57
00:03:32.617 --> 00:03:35.882
The overall score is the average of the four section bands.

58
00:03:36.833 --> 00:03:45.233
Check what your university requires, then study every section. Because Reading and Listening are adaptive, accuracy early in each section matters.

59
00:03:45.983 --> 00:03:50.215
Be careful! Don't say: The overall score is the highest band.

60
00:03:52.167 --> 00:03:55.118
Say: The overall score is the average.

61
00:03:55.418 --> 00:03:57.325
Overall means average.

62
00:03:58.133 --> 00:04:00.553
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:04:01.367 --> 00:04:02.728
My Score Plan.

64
00:04:03.028 --> 00:04:05.875
Sophea wants to apply to a university abroad.

65
00:04:06.867 --> 00:04:10.480
The university asks for an overall band of 5.0.

66
00:04:11.467 --> 00:04:14.140
She learns that Reading and Listening are adaptive.

67
00:04:15.133 --> 00:04:18.317
So she practises accuracy from the very first question.

68
00:04:19.333 --> 00:04:22.343
She plans time for all four sections each week.

69
00:04:23.433 --> 00:04:27.238
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:28.083 --> 00:04:30.687
About how long is the new TOEFL iBT?

71
00:04:30.987 --> 00:04:35.313
A, thirty minutes. B, ninety minutes. C, four hours.

72
00:04:38.867 --> 00:04:41.296
The answer is B: ninety minutes.

73
00:04:42.450 --> 00:04:44.206
Which sections are adaptive?

74
00:04:44.506 --> 00:04:48.658
A, Writing only. B, Speaking only. C, Reading and Listening.

75
00:04:52.200 --> 00:04:54.571
The answer is C: Reading and Listening.

76
00:04:55.717 --> 00:04:57.565
The overall score is blank.

77
00:04:57.865 --> 00:05:03.074
A, the average of four bands. B, the highest band. C, the Reading band.

78
00:05:06.633 --> 00:05:09.411
The answer is A: the average of four bands.

79
00:05:10.550 --> 00:05:12.515
The band scale runs from blank.

80
00:05:12.815 --> 00:05:18.442
A, 10 to 90. B, 1 to 6. C, 0 to 120.

81
00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:24.267
The answer is B: 1 to 6.

82
00:05:25.417 --> 00:05:28.066
What does Sophea's university ask for?

83
00:05:28.366 --> 00:05:33.924
A, a band of 1.0. B, no score. C, a band of 5.0.

84
00:05:37.467 --> 00:05:40.976
The answer is C: a band of 5.0.

85
00:05:42.167 --> 00:05:45.249
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:46.083 --> 00:05:48.454
What score do you need for TOEFL, and why?

87
00:05:57.250 --> 00:05:58.901
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:59.201 --> 00:06:15.057
I need an overall band of 5.0 because my university asks for it. I will learn the format of each section first. Then I will practise a little every week, and I will take timed practice tests to check my progress.

89
00:06:15.357 --> 00:06:16.904
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:06:17.817 --> 00:06:23.418
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and strategy: know the format before you practise.

91
00:06:23.718 --> 00:06:28.170
Today's value is preparedness. Get ready before an emergency happens.

92
00:06:28.470 --> 00:06:31.041
See you in Unit two. Goodbye!

93
00:06:31.341 --> 00:06:33.866
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

